<!DOCTYPE document SYSTEM "http://commons.omniupdate.com/dtd/standard.dtd"> 

<document xmlns:ouc="http://omniupdate.com/XSL/Variables">
	
	<headcode></headcode> <!-- before closing head tag -->
	<bodycode></bodycode> <!-- after opening body tag -->
	<footcode></footcode> <!-- before closing body tag -->
	
	<ouc:info>
		<tcf>interior.tcf</tcf>
		<tmpl>interior.tmpl</tmpl>
	</ouc:info>
	
	<ouc:properties label="config">				
		<parameter name="heading" type="text" group="Everyone" prompt="Page Heading" alt="Enter the page heading text. Not displayed if left blank.">Distance Education</parameter>
		<parameter name="breadcrumb" type="text" group="Everyone" prompt="Breadcrumb" alt="Not displayed for index pages. Page title by default.">Distance Education</parameter>
		<parameter section="Top of Page Media" name="top-media" type="select" group="Everyone" prompt="Banner / Slider" alt="Choose between banner or slider for the top of the page media. Turn it off to hide the banner or use the snippet version.">
<option value="slider" selected="true">Slider</option>
<option value="banner" selected="false">Banner</option>
<option value="off" selected="false">Off</option>
</parameter>

		<parameter section="Banner Properties" name="banner" type="filechooser" group="Everyone" prompt="Banner Image" alt="Select a banner image."></parameter>
		<parameter name="banner-alt" type="text" group="Everyone" prompt="Banner Alt-Text" alt="Enter the alternate text for the banner image."></parameter>

		<parameter section="Page Layout" name="layout" type="select" group="Everyone" prompt="Number of Columns" alt="Switch between two or three column layout.">
<option value="two" selected="true">Two Column</option>
<option value="three" selected="false">Three Column</option>
</parameter>		

		<parameter section="LDP Gallery" name="gallery-type" type="select" group="Everyone" prompt="Gallery Type" alt="Select the output type for gallery assets on this page.">
<option value="flex-slider" selected="true">Flex Slider</option>
<option value="magnific-popup" selected="false">Magnific PopUp</option>
<option value="pretty-photo" selected="false">Pretty Photo</option>
<option value="fancy-box" selected="false">Fancy Box</option>
</parameter>
	</ouc:properties>
	
	<ouc:properties label="metadata">
		<title>Distance Education</title>
		<meta name="Description" content="" />
	</ouc:properties>
	
	<ouc:div label="gallery" group="Everyone" button-text="Select Slider">
		<ouc:editor wysiwyg="gallery" csspath="/_resources/ou/editor/wysiwyg.css" cssmenu="/_resources/ou/editor/styles.txt"/>		
	</ouc:div>
	
	<ouc:div label="main-content" group="Everyone" button-text="Main Content"><ouc:editor csspath="/_resources/ou/editor/wysiwyg.css" cssmenu="/_resources/ou/editor/styles.txt" wysiwyg-class="main-content"/><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://www.ltcc.edu/_resources/images/ltcc_images/academics/online_icon.jpg" alt="Distance Education icon" width="304" height="239" /><br /></span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Classes identified as Distance Education (DE) in LTCC&rsquo;s course schedule are traditional online courses that provide flexibility for students who are adept at setting and keeping their own work pace. While DE classes do provide some structure, they often have no specific class meeting days or times, allowing students to tackle their classwork on their own schedules. LTCC&rsquo;s DE classes typically were originally structured from the beginning to be online classes &ndash; they are not formerly face-to-face classes redeveloped for virtual learning. </span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">While DE classes offer a great deal of flexibility and convenience coupled with high-quality instruction, they also require students to provide their own self-motivation and self-reliance. Classwork is typically required to be done on students&rsquo; own time, without direct faculty supervision. If you are organized and good at planning, DE classes could be perfect for you!</span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a title="Course Schedule" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/scheduleofclasses.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-size: 14pt;">Check out the course schedule&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;</span></a></p></ouc:div>

	<ouc:div label="right-content" group="Everyone" button-text="Right Column Content">
		<ouc:editor csspath="/_resources/ou/editor/wysiwyg.css" cssmenu="/_resources/ou/editor/styles.txt" wysiwyg-class="right-content"/>
		<h2>Edit Title</h2>
		<p>Edit Content</p>
	</ouc:div>
	
</document>
